## THE PARTS (what you build; type and member names in backticks are DEFAULTS of Q14: keep them unless a name collides, and say so)
**P1. Inputs and their checks.** `copyspecs.py --write` (THE TOOLS) into `<clone>`; T4 into `contracts/oxpd2/.gitattributes`. Tests (`InputsTests`): (a) every line of `inputs.sha256` recomputed over the committed file equals; the set of files under `contracts/oxpd2/hp/` equals the set the list names (no extra, none missing); 37 lines; (b) every `$ref` in the 37 files resolves: no external reference in a bundle, every external reference of a target or type names a file in the list and a JSON pointer that exists; print the counts (expected 3819 / 365 / 146 / 0, MEASURED by the drafter's Python, UNMEASURED in your C#). The repository root is found by walking up from `AppContext.BaseDirectory` to the folder holding `Datasec.Suite.slnx`. Each check is a function over a folder argument, so its control (below) can feed it a temp folder.
**P2. The generator and the inbound models (G1).** `contracts/oxpd2/generator/*.cs`, namespace `Datasec.Suite.Contracts.Generator`, entry point `Oxpd2Generator.Generate(string contractsRoot)` returning the ordered list of `(relative path, text)` it would write under `src/Datasec.Suite.Adapters.Oxpd2/Generated/`. It reads documents with `JsonDocument` and `AllowDuplicateProperties = false` (the member exists in the .NET 10 reference pack, MEASURED: `P:System.Text.Json.JsonDocumentOptions.AllowDuplicateProperties` and `P:System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions.AllowDuplicateProperties` in `System.Text.Json.xml` of `packs/Microsoft.NETCore.App.Ref/10.0.15`). **Determinism (both legs must emit the same bytes):** `\n` only, never `Environment.NewLine`; invariant culture; ordinal sorting of every list it emits; no clock, no machine name, no absolute path in any output. **Per service** (`03:141`): one namespace per input document, `Datasec.Suite.Adapters.Oxpd2.Generated.<Service>` for a bundle and `Datasec.Suite.Adapters.Oxpd2.Generated.Targets.<Service>` for a target, where `<Service>` is the folder name after `com.hp.ext.service.` with its first letter upper-cased; a target's reached type schemas are emitted INTO that target's namespace (duplication across namespaces is expected and is the point). **Emitted fixed runtime** (`Generated/Runtime/*.cs`, text inside the generator): `Oxpd2ParseLimits`, `Oxpd2Refusal` (a kind and a JSON path, never a value), `Oxpd2Json.TryParse<T>(ReadOnlySpan<byte> body, Oxpd2ParseLimits limits, out T? value, out Oxpd2Refusal? refusal)` and the one `JsonSerializerOptions` it uses. **Type mapping (Q6):** `object` with `properties` a sealed class, Pascal-cased C# names (which also clears the three keywords) with `[JsonPropertyName("<wire name>")]` on every property (so `$opMeta` maps); `integer` `long`; `string` `string` whatever its format; `boolean` `bool`; `array` `IReadOnlyList<T>`; `additionalProperties` a `IReadOnlyDictionary<string, T>`; `allOf` of one `$ref` the referenced type; `allOf` of refs plus properties one flattened class; `anyOf [ $ref , {} ]` the referenced type (strict, Q6); `oneOf` a `JsonElement` (named limit); `enum` an enum type with `[JsonStringEnumMemberName]` per value, unknown values refused (Q6). **No `description` text of HP's is emitted** (Q7). Generated code compiles warning-free under the repository's `TreatWarningsAsErrors` and nullable settings (`Directory.Build.props` lines 4 and 6, MEASURED at main).
**P3. The gateway stub (test project only).** `GatewayStub` (an `IAsyncDisposable`) starts a `WebApplication` on Kestrel at `http://127.0.0.1:0`, reads back the bound port, and serves exactly the surface report A9 lines 45 to 47 give (RELAYED): `GET /api/healthcheck` 200 with body `Healthy!`; `POST /api/negotiate` 200 with a JSON object holding the stub's own hub address and a SYNTHETIC access token (A9:46: "the SignalR client URL and a short-lived SignalR access token"); `POST /api/send` reads the JSON body and sends ONE hub message to EVERY connection of hub `printerhub`, method name = the body's `realm`, the single argument = the whole body, then 200 with no body; a body that is not JSON: 500 with a JSON `{"error": ...}` (A9:47). The hub is ASP.NET Core SignalR from the shared framework (4 `Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR*.dll` present, MEASURED), mapped at `/printerhub` (Q10). **No SignalR CLIENT package exists in the cache** (MEASURED: 0 entries match `signalr`), so the TEST connects the way the protocol works, by hand, as a named test helper `HubTestClient`: `POST <hub>/negotiate?negotiateVersion=1`, a `ClientWebSocket` to `ws://.../printerhub?id=<connectionToken>`, the JSON handshake `{"protocol":"json","version":1}` followed by the record separator 0x1E, then reading invocation frames (type 1, `target`, `arguments`). Every test `HttpClient` uses a handler with `UseProxy = false`, and the `ClientWebSocket` sets `Options.Proxy = null`: the runner of HEAVY sets `HTTP_PROXY` to a closed port (MEASURED in `heavy.py`), and whether .NET bypasses it for `127.0.0.1` on its own is UNMEASURED. The stub records the `Authorization` header it received (for WP3.1's tests later) and checks none (the deployed gateway's platform demands a tenant token, A9:51: a named limit of the stub). The body used in tests is SYNTHETIC, the seven fields of report A12 line 70 with low-variety values (`printer-0001`, `synthetic-realm-0001`, `synthetic-secret-0001`, `user0001@example.test`, `Given0001`, `Family0001`). **The product project references nothing of ASP.NET Core** (control C8).
**P4. The outbound clients and the regeneration check.** From each of the 16 bundles: one client class per service (`<Service>Client`, constructor takes an `HttpClient` whose base address and handlers are the CALLER's), one `async` method per operation named from its `operationId` (201 in all, Block S), path parameters escaped with `Uri.EscapeDataString`, query parameters likewise, JSON request bodies serialised with the runtime's options, JSON responses parsed through `Oxpd2Json.TryParse` with the SAME limits (a device's answer is network input too), non-JSON bodies passed through raw (Q8). **No token, no `Authorization` header, no retry, no refresh in any client** (`02:362`: WP1.2's). Then `RegenerationTests`: `Oxpd2Generator.Generate(<repo>/contracts/oxpd2)` equals the committed files under `Generated/` byte for byte and as a set (a stale extra file fails). **Writing the files** is done by a small console project in YOUR lane folder, `<lane>/regen/` (never committed): its project file names `net10.0`, `Nullable` and `ImplicitUsings` itself, compiles `<clone>/contracts/oxpd2/generator/**/*.cs` by an absolute `Compile Include`, needs no package, and its `Program.cs` calls `Generate` and writes each file (through a temp file and `os.replace`'s C# twin `File.Move(tmp, path, overwrite: true)`); its build and run are HEAVY jobs. **Size of the generated code: UNMEASURED** (1483 bundle schemas plus the targets' reached schemas, 213 operations; print the file count and bytes of `Generated/` in STATUS).

## THE REQUIRED SECTION: what is the subject handed that is NOT the tested shape?
**The property: every body a printer (inbound, the 10 target operations) or a device answer (outbound, every JSON response) hands to `Oxpd2Json.TryParse` ends in a value or an `Oxpd2Refusal`, never another exception, never an unbounded read, never a refusal or exception message that holds a byte of the body.** At least these, each with its cell (the test class and what it asserts) or a NAMED LIMIT; any other shape you meet: give it a cell or name it as a limit in STATUS, never leave it out. Rows N1 to N14 run against the models of EVERY one of the 10 inbound JSON operations (the payload of each is built by program from its schema, Q11), not one.
| # | The input that is not the tested shape | Cell or named limit |
|---|---|---|
| N1 | **A body far over any size**: exactly `MaxBodyBytes` passes the size check; one byte more; 64 MiB of spaces; 64 MiB of `[` | `InboundLimitTests`: `TooLarge` before ANY JSON read (the test asserts the parser was handed nothing past the check: the size check runs on the span length first); default `MaxBodyBytes` 1048576 (Q6) |
| N2 | **Deep nesting**: depth `MaxDepth` passes; `MaxDepth + 1`; 100000 nested arrays inside a valid prefix | `InboundLimitTests`: `TooDeep`; no `StackOverflowException`, no `InsufficientExecutionStackException` escapes (default `MaxDepth` 32, Q6; the deepest schema is 9, MEASURED) |
| N3 | **An unknown enum value** (a value not in the schema's list; the same value differing only by case) | `InboundShapeTests`: `UnknownEnumValue` with the JSON path (Q6) |
| N4 | **A missing required field**; a required field present as `null` | `InboundShapeTests`: `MissingRequired` with the path |
| N5 | **A duplicate key** at the top level and three levels down | `InboundShapeTests`: `DuplicateKey` (`AllowDuplicateProperties = false`) |
| N6 | **A number out of range**: below `minimum`, above `maximum`; `9223372036854775808` (Int64 + 1); `-9223372036854775809`; `1.5`; `1e3`; `-0` | `InboundShapeTests`: `OutOfRange` for the schema bounds; `WrongType` for the rest (`1e3` and `1.5` are not integers to the parser; `-0` reads as 0: say what yours does) |
| N7 | **A string in a number's place** (`"5"`), a number in a string's place, an object in an array's place, an array at the top level | `InboundShapeTests`: `WrongType` with the path |
| N8 | **Text that is not JSON**: empty body; invalid UTF-8; a comment; a trailing comma; a second value after the first; a BOM; a lone surrogate escape `"\ud800"` | `InboundShapeTests`: `Malformed` (say per row what yours gives for the BOM and the lone surrogate) |
| N9 | **Strings and arrays past their schema bounds**: over `maxLength`, under `minLength`, over `maxItems`, under `minItems`, a map over `maxProperties` | `InboundShapeTests`: `OutOfRange` with the path |
| N10 | **An unknown property** at the top level and nested | `InboundShapeTests`: accepted and IGNORED (Q6 default); the value carries no trace of it |
| N11 | **A non-object where HP's schema says `anyOf [ $ref , {} ]`** (a string, a number, an array) | `InboundShapeTests`: `WrongType` (strict, Q6: a deliberate difference from HP's "anything"; say so in FOR TUESDAY) |
| N12 | **Random bytes** of any length (0 to 4096) and **mutated valid payloads** (one byte flipped, inserted or removed) | `InboundFuzzTests`: a FIXED seed written in the test, at least 20000 inputs per inbound operation (10 operations), no clock, no sleep; each ends in a value or a refusal, never another type; no refusal's `ToString()` holds 4 or more consecutive bytes of its input that are not JSON punctuation |
| N13 | **Hostile path parameters** in an OUTBOUND call: `../x`, `a/b`, `%2F`, a space, `?x=1`, `#`, an empty string, 10000 characters | `ClientRequestTests` with a fake `HttpMessageHandler`: the request path holds each value escaped, never a new path segment or query; empty: `ArgumentException` naming the parameter only |
| N14 | **A device answer** with each of N1 to N9 as its body, and a 200 with no body | `ClientResponseTests`: the same refusals through the client's result; no exception but `ArgumentException`/`OperationCanceledException` leaves a client method |
| N15 | **Things this lane does not check** | NAMED LIMITS: `pattern` is NOT validated (259 patterns; .NET and ECMA regex dialects differ and a backtracking engine on network input is its own risk, Q6); `format` is NOT validated (`uuid`, `date-time`, `uri-reference`, `byte` stay strings); the request STREAM's size cap is the host's (WP1.2: `TryParse` takes a span the host has already bounded); the scan destination's `multipart/mixed` and `*/*` bodies are not parsed (Q16); the callback credential and the token are WP1.2's |

